<div id="q-share-restrictions" class="question">
  <h3>10. How and when will data be shared? Are there possible restrictions to data sharing or embargo reasons?</h3>

  <div class="answer">
    {# How data will be shared #}
    <h4>How the data will be shared</h4>
    {%- if data.dmp.datasets|length == 0 -%}
        <p>There are no datasets described in the {{ globals.projects }}.</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <ul>
    {%- for dataset in data.dmp.datasets -%}
        <li>
        {%- if dataset.name -%}
            <strong>{{ dataset.name._value }}</strong>{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataset.name._path) }}
        {%- else -%}
            <strong>(no name given)</strong>
        {%- endif -%}
        {# If will be published #}
        {%- if dataset.willBePublished and dataset.willBePublished._value is sameas true -%}
            {%- if dataset.isPublished and dataset.isPublished._value is sameas true %} (published){{ macros.linkQuestion(dataset.isPublished._path) }}
            {%- elif dataset.isPublished and dataset.isPublished._value is sameas false %} (will be published){{ macros.linkQuestion(dataset.isPublished._path) }}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- elif dataset.willBePublished and dataset.willBePublished._value is sameas false %}
            (will not be published){{ macros.linkQuestion(dataset.willBePublished._path) }}
        {%- endif -%}:
        {# Identifiers #}
        {%- if dataset.metadata -%}
            {%- set metadata = data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications|selectattr("uuid", "equalto", dataset.metadata)|first -%}
            {%- if metadata.usesPids -%}
                {%- if metadata.usesPids._value is sameas true -%}
                    {%- if metadata.whoProvidesPids and metadata.whoProvidesPids._value -%}
                        <p>
                        {%- if metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "project" -%}
                            A persistent identifier (PID) for this dataset will be assigned by the project’s data steward or principal investigator.
                        {%- elif metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "institutional" -%}
                            A persistent identifier (PID) for this dataset will be assigned by the institutional data steward.
                        {%- elif metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "repository" -%}
                            A persistent identifier (PID) for this dataset will be assigned automatically by the data repository upon submission.
                        {%- elif metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "provider" -%}
                            A persistent identifier (PID) for this dataset will be assigned by the national or international PID service provider.
                        {%- else -%}
                            A persistent identifier (PID) for this dataset will be assigned by {{ metadata.whoProvidesPids._value }}.
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.whoProvidesPids._path) }}
                        </p>
                    {%- endif -%}
                {%- elif metadata.usesPids._value is sameas false -%}
                    <p>A persistent identifier (PID) for this dataset will not be assigned.{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.usesPids._path) }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if dataset.identifiers|length > 0 %}
            <p>The dataset has the following identifiers:
            <ul>
                {%- for identifier in dataset.identifiers -%}
                    <li>
                    {{ macros.formatIdentifier(identifier) }}
                    </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
            </p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {# Distributions #}
        {%- if dataset.distributions|length > 0 -%}
            <p>This dataset has {{ dataset.distributions|length }} distribution{{ 's' if dataset.distributions|length != 1 else '' }}:
            <ul>
            {%- for distribution in dataset.distributions -%}
                <li>
                    {%- if distribution.name -%}
                        <strong>{{ distribution.name._value }}</strong>{{ macros.linkQuestion(distribution.name._path) }}
                    {%- else -%}
                        <strong>(no distribution name given)</strong>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {# Sharing mode #}
                    {%- if distribution.technicalAvailability.accessMode -%}
                        {%- if distribution.technicalAvailability.accessMode._value == "open" %}
                            will be shared openly (available to anyone){{ macros.linkQuestion(distribution.technicalAvailability.accessMode._path) }}.
                        {%- elif distribution.technicalAvailability.accessMode._value == "shared" %}
                            will be shared with specific individuals or groups{{ macros.linkQuestion(distribution.technicalAvailability.accessMode._path) }}.
                        {%- elif distribution.technicalAvailability.accessMode._value == "closed" %}
                            will be shared in a closed manner (e.g., with a specific project team){{ macros.linkQuestion(distribution.technicalAvailability.accessMode._path) }}.
                        {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {# When published? #}
                    {%- if distribution.whenAvailable -%}
                        <p>
                        {%- if distribution.whenAvailable.isAvailableImmediately and distribution.whenAvailable.isAvailableImmediately._value is sameas true %}
                            This distribution will be published as soon as possible after it has been collected.{{ macros.linkQuestion(distribution.whenAvailable.isAvailableImmediately._path) }}
                        {%- elif distribution.whenAvailable.isAvailableImmediately and distribution.whenAvailable.isAvailableImmediately._value is sameas false -%}
                            {%- set postponedAvailability = distribution.whenAvailable.postponedAvailability %}
                            This distribution will not be available immediately after it has been collected.{{ macros.linkQuestion(distribution.whenAvailable.isAvailableImmediately._path) }}
                            {%- if postponedAvailability.isExactStartDateKnown -%}
                                {%- if postponedAvailability.isExactStartDateKnown._value is sameas true and postponedAvailability.exactStartDate %}
                                    It will be available starting from {{ postponedAvailability.exactStartDate._value if postponedAvailability.exactStartDate._value else "an unknown date" }}.{{ macros.linkQuestion(postponedAvailability.exactStartDate._path) }}
                                {%- elif postponedAvailability.isExactStartDateKnown._value is sameas false and postponedAvailability.availabilityDelayAfterProjectEnd %}
                                    It will be available {{ postponedAvailability.availabilityDelayAfterProjectEnd._value if postponedAvailability.availabilityDelayAfterProjectEnd._value else "at a later date" }} after the end of the project.{{ macros.linkQuestion(postponedAvailability.availabilityDelayAfterProjectEnd._path) }}
                                {%- endif -%}
                            {%- endif -%}
                            {%- if postponedAvailability.isEmbargoPeriod -%}
                                {%- if postponedAvailability.isEmbargoPeriod._value is sameas true %}
                                    There will be an embargo period{{ macros.linkQuestion(postponedAvailability.isEmbargoPeriod._path) }}
                                    {%- if postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod -%}
                                        {%- if postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.durationEmbargoPeriod and postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.durationEmbargoPeriod._value %}
                                            of {{ postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.durationEmbargoPeriod._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.durationEmbargoPeriod._path) }}
                                        {%- endif -%}
                                        {%- if postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.reason and postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.reason._value %}
                                            (reason: {{ postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.reason._value }}){{ macros.linkQuestion(postponedAvailability.embargoPeriod.reason._path) }}
                                        {%- endif -%}.
                                    {%- endif -%}
                                {%- elif postponedAvailability.isEmbargoPeriod._value is sameas false and postponedAvailability.noEmbargoReasonForPostponedAvailability %}
                                    There is no embargo period; the postponed availability is due to: {{ postponedAvailability.noEmbargoReasonForPostponedAvailability._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(postponedAvailability.noEmbargoReasonForPostponedAvailability._path) }}.
                                {%- endif -%}
                            {%- endif -%}
                        {%- else %}
                            The availability date for this distribution has not been specified.
                        {%- endif -%}
                        </p>
                    {%- endif -%}

                    {# Free and Standard Protocol #}
                    {%- if distribution.technicalAvailability -%}
                        {%- set technicalAvailability = distribution.technicalAvailability -%}
                        {%- if technicalAvailability.isAccessibleViaStandardProtocol -%}
                            {%- if technicalAvailability.isAccessibleViaStandardProtocol._value is sameas true -%}
                                <p>This distribution will be accessible via a standard protocol{{ macros.linkQuestion(technicalAvailability.isAccessibleViaStandardProtocol._path) }}
                                {%- if technicalAvailability.usedStandardProtocol._value %} ({{ technicalAvailability.usedStandardProtocol._value }}){{ macros.linkQuestion(technicalAvailability.usedStandardProtocol._path) }}
                                {%- endif -%}.</p>
                            {%- elif technicalAvailability.isAccessibleViaStandardProtocol._value is sameas false -%}
                                <p>This distribution will not be accessible via a standard protocol{{ macros.linkQuestion(technicalAvailability.isAccessibleViaStandardProtocol._path) }}
                                {%- if technicalAvailability.notAccessibleViaStandardProtocolReason._value %} because: {{ technicalAvailability.notAccessibleViaStandardProtocolReason._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(technicalAvailability.notAccessibleViaStandardProtocolReason._path) }}{%- endif -%}.</p>
                            {%- endif -%}
                        {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}

                    {# Licenses #}
                    {%- if distribution.isLicenseAssignedForDistribution -%}
                        <p>
                        {%- if distribution.isLicenseAssignedForDistribution._value is sameas true -%}
                            {%- set licensing = distribution.licensing -%}
                            {%- if licensing.isLicenseChosen and licensing.isLicenseChosen._value is sameas true and licensing.licenses|length > 0 -%}
                                The distribution will be available under the following {{ "licenses" if licensesItems|length > 1 else "license" }}:
                                <ul>
                                {%- for license in licensing.licenses -%}
                                    <li>
                                        {%- if license.license and license.license._raw -%}
                                            <strong><a href="{{ license.license._raw.url }}" target="_blank">{{ license.license._raw.name }}</a></strong>{{ macros.linkQuestion(license.license._path) }}
                                        {%- elif license.license -%}
                                            <strong>{{ license.license._value }}</strong>{{ macros.linkQuestion(license.license._path) }}
                                        {%- else -%}
                                            <strong>(no name given):</strong>
                                        {%- endif -%}
                                        {%- if license.startDate -%}
                                            <br>Start date: {{ license.startDate._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(license.startDate._path) }}
                                        {%- endif -%}
                                    </li>
                                {%- endfor -%}
                                </ul>

                            {%- elif licensing.isLicenseChosen and licensing.isLicenseChosen._value is sameas false %}
                                No license has been selected for this distribution yet.{{ macros.linkQuestion(licensing.isLicenseChosen._path) }}
                                {%- if licensing.notYetDecidedLicense -%}
                                    {%- if licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.isOpenLicense -%}
                                        {%- if licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.isOpenLicense._value is sameas true %}
                                            {%- if licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.licenseBasedOnLicenseSelector %}
                                                {%- set license = licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.licenseBasedOnLicenseSelector %}
                                                However, we plan to use and open license and, based the recommendations from the <a href="https://github.com/ufal/public-license-selector" target="_blank" rel="noopener">License Selector</a>, we are considering the following license: <em><a href="{{ license._raw.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ license._raw.name }}</a></em>.{{ macros.linkQuestion(license._path) }}
                                            {%- else %}
                                                We plan to use an open license for this distribution.{{ macros.linkQuestion(licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.isOpenLicense._path) }}
                                            {%- endif -%}
                                        {%- elif licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.isOpenLicense._value is sameas false %}
                                            We do not plan to use an open license for this distribution{{ macros.linkQuestion(licensing.notYetDecidedLicense._path) }} {%- if licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.noOpenLicenseReason %} because: {{ licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.noOpenLicenseReason._value }}.{{ macros.linkQuestion(licensing.notYetDecidedLicense.noOpenLicenseReason._path) }}{%- else -%}.{%- endif -%}
                                        {%- endif -%}
                                    {%- endif -%}
                                {%- endif -%}
                            {%- else -%}
                                We plan to assign a license to this distribution, but it has not been specified yet.{{ macros.linkQuestion(licensing.isLicenseChosen._path) }}
                            {%- endif -%}
                        {%- elif distribution.isLicenseAssignedForDistribution._value is sameas false -%}
                            No license specified for this distribution.{{ macros.linkQuestion(distribution.isLicenseAssignedForDistribution._path) }}
                        {%- endif -%}
                        </p>
                    {%- endif -%}
                </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
            </p>
        {%- else -%}
            <p>This dataset has no distributions defined yet.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    {# Repository #}
    <h4>Where the data will be shared</h4>
    {%- if data.dmp.sharedResources.dataStores|length == 0 -%}
        <p>No data repositories have been specified for sharing the data.</p>
    {%- else -%}
        <p>Below, the individual distributions are listed together with information on the repositories in which they will be stored or shared.</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <ul>
    {%- for dataStorage in data.dmp.sharedResources.dataStores -%}
        <li>
        <em>
            {%- if dataStorage.name -%}
                {%- if dataStorage.name._raw -%}
                    <a href="https://fairsharing.org/{{ dataStorage.name._raw.id }}" target="_blank">{{ dataStorage.name._raw.name }}</a>{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.name._path) }}
                {%- elif dataStorage.name._value -%}
                    {{ dataStorage.name._value }}{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.name._path) }}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- else -%}
                (no name given)
            {%- endif -%}
        </em>
        {% if dataStorage.type|length > 0 %} (
            {%- for type in dataStorage.type -%}
                {{ type._label|lower }}{{ ", " if not loop.last else "" }}
            {%- endfor -%}) {% endif %}

        {%- if dataStorage.usedBy|length > 0 -%}
            <p>The following repository will be used to share the following distributions:</p>
            {%- for distributionUuid in dataStorage.usedBy -%}
                {%- for datasetItem in data.dmp.datasets -%}
                    <ul>
                    {%- for distributionItem in datasetItem.distributions -%}
                        {%- if distributionItem.uuid == distributionUuid -%}
                        <li>
                            {%- if distributionItem.name -%}
                            <em>{{ distributionItem.name._value }}</em>{{ macros.linkQuestion(distributionItem.name._path) }}
                            {%- else -%}
                                <em>(no distribution name given)</em>
                            {%- endif -%}
                        </li>
                        {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                    </ul>
                {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
            <p>No distributions have been assigned to this repository yet.</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if dataStorage.storage -%}
            {# Certification #}
            {%- if dataStorage.storage.isCertified or dataStorage.storage.supportsVersioning  -%}
                The repository
                {% if dataStorage.storage.isCertified._value is sameas true %}
                    is certified{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.certification._path) }}{%- if dataStorage.storage.certification %} ({{ dataStorage.storage.certification._label if dataStorage.storage.certification._label else dataStorage.storage.certification._value if dataStorage.storage.certification._value }}){{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.certification._path) }}{%- endif -%}
                {% elif dataStorage.storage.isCertified._value is sameas false %}
                    is not certified{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.certification._path) }}
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if dataStorage.storage.isCertified and dataStorage.storage.supportsVersioning %} and{%- elif dataStorage.storage.isCertified -%}.{% endif %}

                {# Versioning #}
                {% if dataStorage.storage.supportsVersioning._value is sameas true %}
                    supports versioning of the data.{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.supportsVersioning._path) }}
                {% elif dataStorage.storage.supportsVersioning._value is sameas false %}
                    does not support versioning of the data.{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.supportsVersioning._path) }}
                {% endif %}
            {%- endif -%}

            {# PID systems #}
            {% if dataStorage.storage.pidSystems|length > 0 %}
                It uses the following persistent identifier system{% if dataStorage.storage.pidSystems|length > 1 %}s{% endif %}: {{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.pidSystems[0]._path) }}
                <em>
                {%- for pidSystemItem in dataStorage.storage.pidSystems -%}
                    {%- if pidSystemItem.pidSystem._raw -%}
                        {{ pidSystemItem.pidSystem._raw.name  }} - {{ pidSystemItem.pidSystem._raw.homepage }}
                    {%- elif pidSystemItem.pidSystem._value -%}
                        {{ pidSystemItem.pidSystem._value }}
                    {%- else -%}
                        (no name given)
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{ ", " if not loop.last else "" }}
                {%- endfor -%}
                </em>
                {# Resolvable PID #}
                {% if dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._value is sameas true %}
                    with resolvable persistent identifiers.{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._path) }}
                {% elif dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._value is sameas false %}
                    but does not use resolvable persistent identifiers.{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._path) }}
                {% endif %}
            {% else %}
                {% if dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._value is sameas true %}
                    It supports resolvable persistent identifiers.{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._path) }}
                {% elif dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._value is sameas false %}
                    It does not support resolvable persistent identifiers.{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.storage.resolvablePid._path) }}
                {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
        {%- endif -%}

        {# Repository requirements #}
        {%- if dataStorage.agreementOnStorageInfrastructureUse -%}
            Accessing and using the hosting infrastructure may require following steps and agreements: {{ dataStorage.agreementOnStorageInfrastructureUse._value if dataStorage.agreementOnStorageInfrastructureUse._value else "(no details provided)" }}.{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataStorage.agreementOnStorageInfrastructureUse._path) }}
        {%- endif -%}

        </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    {# Restrictions #}
    <h4>Restrictions on data sharing</h4>
    <p>Ethical and legal restrictions are documented under Section 4. We have used the {{ dc.config.service_name }}, which made us aware of options to minimize the restrictions.</p>
  </div>
</div>
